**Issue**: #93
**Date**: 2026-09-06
**Status**: Approved
**Author**: NMG

Feature: Greeting word-count lifecycle fixture
  @AC1
  Scenario Outline: Count words in the greeting
    Given the name "<name>"
    When I call the exported greeting_word_count helper
    Then the word count is <count>
    Examples:
      | name         | count |
      | Ada          | 2     |
      | Ada Lovelace | 3     |

  @AC2
  Scenario: Preserve greeting validation
    Given blank, whitespace-only, or non-string input
    When I call greeting_word_count
    Then it raises the existing greet ValueError
    And existing greeting and CLI contracts remain unchanged

  @AC3
  Scenario: Independently verify the fixture
    Given the documented public helper and behavior tests
    When the existing pytest, pytest-bdd, and Ruff checks run
    Then all checks pass without relaxing unrelated contracts
